# THE NEVER-LIST — one path pattern per line, shell-glob syntax, matched against repo-relative paths.
#
# ⛔ THIS IS THE ONLY COPY THAT MATTERS. Read by:
#   · bin/hooks/reference-transaction  — installed into the COMMON hooks dir, fires on the ref update a
#     commit performs, so it catches `/usr/bin/git commit` and survives `--no-verify`.
#   · the PATH wrapper (coder-bin/git today, bin/coder-git next) — catches it earlier, at add/rm/commit,
#     with a message a coder can act on.
# ⚠️ The wrapper still carries its own inline copies as of 2026-09-28; unifying them is a separate commit,
# because the owner's order is hook first, wrapper move second, wrapper rewrite after that. Until then this
# file is authoritative for the HOOK only, and the two are seeded identical on purpose.
#
# MARKERS, and they exist because the wrapper has always had these exemptions — a hook that ignored them
# would refuse work the contract permits:
#   ⚠️ Every @self-edit line also carries @merge-exempt, and it must: without it a lane could never merge a
#      main that changed a guard or supervisor file, because a merge touches other paths and is therefore
#      never 'alone'. Measured 2026-09-28 (N314) — a lane's take-main was refused on 'bin/never-list' itself.
#      A gated merge (GOAIEZ_MERGE_OK=1 + MERGE_HEAD) is exactly how main's guards reach a lane, which is
#      already coder-bin/git:160's policy; a fast-forward is skipped by the reachability test regardless.
#   @self-edit     — committable, but ONLY in a commit that touches nothing outside the @self-edit paths.
#                    This is how the supervisor keeps its own column (CLAUDE.md, bin/supervise.sh, the list
#                    and this hook) amendable by a commit on main, while a coder gutting a guard and
#                    smuggling product in the same commit is still refused.
#   ⛔ OVERLAPPING PATTERNS: the hook evaluates EVERY entry and refuses on ANY unexempt match — it does NOT
#      stop at the most specific one. So a path needs its exemption on EVERY pattern that matches it.
#      Measured 2026-09-28 (N318): `app/app/Doctor/*` carried @merge-exempt while the later `*seals.json`
#      carried none, and a lane take-main was refused on app/app/Doctor/seals.json. My own python model of
#      this file broke on first match and reported "all OK" — the hook was right and the model lied.
#   @merge-exempt  — admissible in a gated merge (GOAIEZ_MERGE_OK=1 and MERGE_HEAD present). ⭐ EVERY pattern
#      carries this, and that is deliberate: this list exists to stop a coder AUTHORING a change to one of
#      these paths, and a gated merge is never authoring — it is adopting main's copy. The hook keeps full
#      force on an authored commit, which has no MERGE_HEAD, and that is the case N313 was written for.
#      coder-bin/git enforces BYTE-IDENTITY to MERGE_HEAD, so a lane still cannot smuggle an edit through a
#      merge; the hook does not check bytes and does not need to. ⛔ Marking them one at a time as each broke
#      a lane was whack-a-mole: .gitattributes, source/*, .env* were all the next failure waiting.
#                    a main that moved these paths MUST be able to carry them; that is coder-bin/git:160.
#   @main-exempt   — admissible in the grs-antig checkout only. coder-bin/git:95 clears the harness needle
#                    by repo name, so Track 1 commits the harness without a flag and always has.
#
.claude                                           @merge-exempt
.claude/*                                         @merge-exempt @self-edit
.agents/supervisor                                @merge-exempt
.agents/supervisor/*                              @merge-exempt @self-edit
.agents/rules                                     @merge-exempt
.agents/rules/*                                   @merge-exempt @self-edit
.agents/state                                     @merge-exempt
.agents/state/*                                   @merge-exempt @self-edit
.agents/workflows/*                               @merge-exempt @self-edit
.agents/skills/*                                  @merge-exempt @self-edit
CLAUDE.md                                         @merge-exempt @self-edit
bin/supervise.sh                                  @merge-exempt @self-edit
bin/state.py                                      @merge-exempt @self-edit
bin/never-list                                    @merge-exempt @self-edit
bin/hooks/*                                       @merge-exempt @self-edit
bin/coder-git                                     @merge-exempt @self-edit
# app/phpunit.xml — REMOVED FROM THIS LIST 2026-09-28 (N314), and the reason is the whole point:
#   it is UNTRACKED on main as of 2e948aeb6, so this hook has nothing left to protect — and while it
#   was listed, the hook REFUSED every lane's take-main, because such a merge DELETES the path and a
#   deletion is a change like any other. Measured, not reasoned: a two-ahead lane merging a main that
#   had untracked it got `rc=128 · fatal: ref updates aborted by hook`. @self-edit cannot help, because
#   a merge touches other paths and so is never 'alone'.
#   ⛔ RULE: a path being removed from tracking comes off this list IN THE SAME ACT as the untracking,
#   or this hook blocks the very merges that carry the removal.
#   Still protected where it matters: coder-bin/git's add and rm arms refuse `git add app/phpunit.xml`,
#   so a coder cannot put it back under version control.
app/app/Doctor                                    @merge-exempt
app/app/Doctor/*                                  @merge-exempt
app/tests/Journeys                                @merge-exempt
app/tests/Journeys/*                              @merge-exempt @main-exempt
*seals.json                                       @merge-exempt
.gitattributes                                    @merge-exempt
.env                                              @merge-exempt
*/.env                                            @merge-exempt
.env.*                                            @merge-exempt
*/.env.*                                          @merge-exempt
source                                            @merge-exempt
source/*                                          @merge-exempt
runtime                                           @merge-exempt
runtime/*                                         @merge-exempt
